  "_comment": "Categories are the knowledge domains crew specialise in. Tiers are the product grade, 1 to 5: each tier declares a colour, the standing a city demands before it will sell that grade to you (total across every segment), the price-per-volume floor every good of that tier must clear (higher tier = denser value, enforced by the loader), and how far its resting stock shrinks (rare goods do not sit in piles of 150). Quality knobs live here so a retune does not require C#: a fresh crate grades base + random(0..random) + the city craft vital x cityVitalWeight/100; nominal is the grade that sells at 1.0x.",

